=== 2b. ARM 2 -- p=1 TILT APPLIED TO THE FABRIC'S OWN PHASES ===
  weight w = |cos(phi_B - b)|   (circle form of rho_1 ~ |lambda.b|)
    max|S| = 2.836696   (Tsirelson 2.828427)   E(0,0) = -1.000000
    <w> = eta = 0.636620   discarded = 0.363380
  This is the ONLY way the fabric's measured phases reach 2sqrt2,
  and it reaches it by throwing away 36.3% of the pairs. Under
  CRANK2 Reading 2 that is the detection loophole: eta = 0.6366 sits
  below both 2(sqrt2-1) = 0.8284 and the Eberhard/CH 2/3 = 0.6667.
  Not a violation -- a demonstration of the price.

=== 3. DISCARD FRACTION ===
  frames read = 167   used = 167   discarded = 0   fraction = 0.000000
  readout weight: every used frame contributes with weight 1 and
  every (a,b) pair yields an outcome -- eta = 1.000000, no
  post-selection on the settings, so no detection loophole is
  available. This is the condition under which |S| <= 2 is a
  genuine tripwire rather than a statement about efficiency.

=== 4. SEARCH-BIAS NULL  (12 replicas, M=167 each) ===
  Synthetic ensembles: lambda drawn uniform, Delta bootstrapped
  from the MEASURED distribution, then run through the identical
  estimator and the identical 360^3 search.

  WHY ARM 1'S NULL MUST COME OUT AT ZERO, AND WHY THAT IS A RESULT:
  this tool builds the FULL 2D table E(a,b) from one consistent set
  of M frames, so all four CHSH terms are averages over the SAME
  samples. For each individual frame the bracket
      A(a)B(b) + A(a)B(b') + A(a')B(b) - A(a')B(b')
  is a sum of four +/-1 products that is algebraically confined to
  {-2,+2}. The sample mean of numbers in [-2,2] cannot leave [-2,2].
  So |S| <= 2 holds EXACTLY, at every M, with no statistical slack
  at all -- a nonzero null here would mean the estimator is broken.
  Contrast bell_grid, whose 1D E(theta) table assumes translation
  invariance of the lambda histogram: its four terms come from
  INCONSISTENT effective samples, the pointwise argument fails, and
  its arm 1 null is +3.95/sqrt(N) (12/12 positive). Same inequality,
  two estimators, only one of which can manufacture a violation.
